From fca36ac472e728f4f1af7ac4f22bb3f8d402eb3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:34:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(background-agent): let runtime-fallback own session.error
 recovery before the task is finalized

A subagent session whose first generation failed (for example
ProviderModelNotFoundError) can be retried by runtime-fallback inside the same
session. The background manager runs before runtime-fallback in the event
dispatcher and finalizes the task as error on a terminal session.error, so the
caller's task handle reports a dead task while the retry generation keeps
working unobserved. If the manager also has a fallback chain, it starts a
replacement session, leaving two writers on the same work.

Each session.error now carries a claim keyed by the event object: the
dispatcher opens it before any hook runs, runtime-fallback settles it as
retry-owned or declined once it has decided, and the manager awaits it before
its own fallback or terminal finalization. Keying by event, not by session or
message id, attributes an error to its own generation even when retry prompts
reuse the original message id. A retry that later fails raises a new
session.error with its own claim, so it can still end the task. Without a
runtime-fallback hook no claim is opened and nothing waits; an unsettled claim
resolves as declined after 20s.
